.TH QMAPSHACK 1 "July 2014" "" ""
.SH NAME
QMapShack \- GPS mapping (GeoTiff and vector) and GPSr management
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqmapshack\fP [\fIoptions\fP] [\fIfiles\fP ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
GPS mapping (GeoTiff and vector) and GPSr management.
QMapShack provides a versatile tool for GPS maps in GeoTiff format as well as Garmin's img vector map format.
You can also view and edit your GPX tracks. QMapShack is the successor of QLandkarteGT.
.TP
Main features:
  \- Use of several workspaces.
  \- Use several maps on a workspace.
  \- Handle data project-oriented.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIfile\fR
Read and write the configuration in \fIfile\fR instead of the user's own.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-debug\fR
Print debug output to the console.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-logfile\fR
Print debug output to a logfile.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Displays the help message.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-locale\fR \fIcode\fR
Application locale, for example \fBde\fR or \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-no\-splash\fR
Start without splash screen.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Displays version information.
.TP
\fB\-\-font\-family\fR \fIname\fR
Application font family.
.TP
\fB\-\-font\-size\fR \fIsize\fR
Application font size, in points.
.TP
\fB\-\-style\fR \fIname\fR
Qt style. \fBFusion\fR is recommended; \fB\-\-help\fR lists what this build offers.
.SS Documentation images
These render the images of the user documentation. They are driven by \fBdoc/tools/shots.py\fR
in the source tree, which composes the configuration and pins the font, style and locale, and
are not meant to be used directly.
.TP
\fB\-\-shoot\fR \fIdir\fR
Render documentation images into \fIdir\fR and exit. Needs \fB\-platform offscreen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-shoot\-task\fR \fItask\fR
What \fB\-\-shoot\fR does: \fBchapter\fR (default) one chapter file, \fBlist\fR the widget
classes a shot can build from nothing, \fBinspect\fR one widget's children and properties, or
\fBexplore\fR which of its controls change it.
.TP
\fB\-\-shoot\-target\fR \fIfile-or-id\fR
What the task works on: the chapter file for \fBchapter\fR, the exposure name for \fBinspect\fR
and \fBexplore\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-shoot\-scenario\fR \fIname\fR
Take only the pictures of the chapter that are taken in this scenario. A scenario carries its own
settings, so one run covers one scenario.
.TP
\fB\-\-only\fR \fIglob\fR
Restrict the run to the images whose id matches \fIglob\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-doc\fR \fIdir\fR
Documentation mode: load the example data and record images into the checkout at \fIdir\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-doc\-chapter\fR \fIname\fR
Which chapter documentation mode records into. Default: \fBscratch\fR.
